<title>USA: Medi-Ject ships advanced system.</title>
<headline>Medi-Ject ships advanced system.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medi-Ject Corp said Wednesday in began initial shipments of its advanced Medi-Jector Choice needle-free insulin injection system for delivery of insulin by persons with diabetes.</p>
<p>The new device features a disposable needle-free syringe that replaces the stainless steel drug chamber, which required frequent cleaning.</p>
<p>Medi-Ject said its new syringe, which has received marketing clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration, allows persons to self-administer 14 injections before discarding the syringe.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
